WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.822
The model asks for a command with a

00:00:02.822 --> 00:00:05.394
typo. OpenCode runs it, and the validator exits

00:00:05.394 --> 00:00:08.288
with an error. That failure becomes a saved learning.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.653
We check the correction and compile it with

00:00:12.653 --> 00:00:15.656
Terraphim. The exported knowledge graph uses synonyms syntax.

00:00:15.656 --> 00:00:19.035
Saving a suggestion alone does not switch rewriting on.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:25.072
In a fresh session, the model requests the typo again. Terraphim returns

00:00:25.072 --> 00:00:29.795
the correction. The adapter applies it, and OpenCode executes the corrected command.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.858
The execution record keeps the original request, the final command, and rule

00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:40.566
one. A hash identifies the exact compiled graph used for this execution.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:45.126
The tool exits successfully. Its result and saved

00:00:45.126 --> 00:00:48.700
file carry the same execution identifier. The receipt also

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:52.273
records the file hash, so changed bytes are detected.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:57.145
Regression tests pass. A separate verifier checks the real

00:00:57.145 --> 00:01:00.640
host events, rule snapshot, result and file together. Download

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.523
the example to repeat the run and inspect the evidence.
